
Transaction Classifier Microservice

A robust, production-ready microservice for text-based classification tasks (e.g., transaction categorization) with online/batch training, batch inference, monitoring, and extensibility.
Features

    FastAPI HTTP API with OpenAPI docs

    Thread-safe training and inference

    Batch and online learning endpoints

    Batch inference endpoint

    Dynamic label set and growing tokenizer

    Model versioning and persistence

    Custom error handling and input validation

    Training metrics (loss, accuracy)

    Data drift monitoring (simple input stats)

    Optional API key security

    Graceful shutdown with signal handling

    Resource management (batch size, timeouts)

    Comprehensive tests

    Docker-ready

Quickstart
1. Build and Run

docker build -t transaction-classifier .
docker run -p 8000:8000 transaction-classifier

Or run locally:

pip install -r requirements.txt
uvicorn main:app --reload

2. API Documentation

Visit http://localhost:8000/docs for interactive API docs.
API Endpoints
Health Check

GET /health

Single Prediction

POST /predict

Request:

{
  "current_transaction": {
    "description": "Starbucks coffee",
    "name": "SBX",
    "merchant": "Starbucks",
    "amount": "4.50"
  },
  "user_history": []
}

Response:

{
  "predicted_category": "coffee",
  "confidence": 0.98
}

Batch Prediction

POST /batch_predict

Request:

{
  "requests": [
    {
      "current_transaction": { ... },
      "user_history": []
    },
    ...
  ]
}

Response:

{
  "results": [
    {"predicted_category": "coffee", "confidence": 0.98},
    ...
  ]
}

Batch Training

POST /train

Request:

{
  "data": [
    {
      "current_transaction": { ... },
      "user_history": []
    }
  ],
  "labels": ["coffee"]
}

Response:

{
  "status": "training_complete",
  "loss": 0.123,
  "accuracy": 1.0
}

Online Learning

POST /online_learn

Request:

{
  "input": {
    "current_transaction": { ... },
    "user_history": []
  },
  "label": "coffee"
}

Response:

{
  "status": "online_learning_complete",
  "loss": 0.05
}

Configuration

Set environment variables or edit config.py:

    MODEL_DIR: Directory for model files (default: ./models)

    TOKENIZER_PATH: Path for tokenizer (default: ./tokenizer.json)

    LABELS_PATH: Path for label mapping (default: ./labels.json)

    API_KEY: (Optional) Set to require API key in requests

    MAX_BATCH_SIZE: Max batch size for batch inference (default: 32)

    REQUEST_TIMEOUT: Request timeout in seconds (default: 30)

Testing

pytest test_main.py

Graceful Shutdown

The service saves model, tokenizer, and labels on SIGTERM/SIGINT (e.g., Docker stop, Ctrl+C).
Extending

    Change input schema in schemas.py for new data types.

    Swap model in model.py for more advanced architectures.

    Add metrics, monitoring, or hooks as needed.

